-- title:
--   Trace radical and reducedness of a cyclic single-root algebra
-- statement:
--   Let K be a field and A a finite-dimensional commutative K-algebra. Let x in A and z,c in K, with c nonzero. Assume polynomial evaluation at x is surjective, and for every polynomial q,
--
--   1. the trace of multiplication by q(x) is c q(z);
--   2. q(x) is nilpotent if and only if q(z)=0.
--
--   Then an element a of A satisfies Tr(ab)=0 for every b in A if and only if a is nilpotent. Consequently, the trace pairing is nondegenerate if and only if A is reduced (has no nonzero nilpotent elements).
--
--   The scalar c is explicitly required to be nonzero; no characteristic-zero assumption is hidden in the statement.
-- source:
--   Derived supporting algebra for the Senthil Kumar mission. For a finite-dimensional commutative K-algebra generated by x, assume trace(L_q(x))=c*q(z) with c nonzero, and q(x) is nilpotent exactly when q(z)=0. Then the radical of the trace pairing consists exactly of nilpotent elements, and the pairing is nondegenerate exactly when the algebra is reduced. This is inferred supporting algebra, not a separately quoted theorem from the source article. Pinned Mathlib revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474: Algebra.traceForm_apply and Algebra.traceForm_isSymm in RingTheory/Trace/Defs.lean; LinearMap.IsRefl.nondegenerate_iff_separatingLeft in LinearAlgebra/SesquilinearForm/Basic.lean; isReduced_iff in Algebra/GroupWithZero/Basic.lean. Primary documentation: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/Trace/Defs.html . No new definitions or platform dependencies.

import Mathlib.RingTheory.Trace.Defs
import Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Algebra

open Polynomial

theorem WeierstrassEllipticZeta.polynomial_cyclic_trace_radical
    (K A : Type*) [Field K] [CommRing A] [Algebra K A] [FiniteDimensional K A]
    (x : A) (z c : K) (hc : c ≠ 0)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (fun q : Polynomial K => q.eval₂ (algebraMap K A) x))
    (htrace : ∀ q : Polynomial K,
      LinearMap.trace K A (Algebra.lmul K A (q.eval₂ (algebraMap K A) x)) = c * q.eval z)
    (hnil : ∀ q : Polynomial K, IsNilpotent (q.eval₂ (algebraMap K A) x) ↔ q.eval z = 0) :
    (∀ a : A, (∀ b : A, Algebra.traceForm K A a b = 0) ↔ IsNilpotent a) ∧
      ((Algebra.traceForm K A).Nondegenerate ↔ IsReduced A) := by sorry
